    ["比煤灰更厚重的黑夜里，唯有工厂区的酒馆保持着喧闹。\n大笑、咳嗽、无休止的抱怨……巡警咒骂着，像避开麻烦一样绕过噪音，走向远处的街区。\n“他们走了。”娜塔放下帘子，向清醒的人们宣告。\n工人们正把布条铺在地上，用木炭条写着明天要举的口号：“要工资”“要休息”“要像人一样生活”，孩子挤在角落，分装干粮与小瓶酒精。烛火昏暗，映出一双双发亮的眼睛。\n“等到明天，我们就能拿回应得的报酬了吗？”年长的工人问。\n“等到明天，我们就能保证十小时的休息吗？”年幼的孩子问。\n“……抱歉，我无法向你们担保。”娜塔沉默了。\n“我们的旗帜会倒下，但我们前进的每一步，都会在地上留下痕迹。”\n或许，远在另一个时代，已经有人沿着它走到天亮。"] = "In the night, heavier than coal dust, only the taverns in the factory district remained noisy. \nLaughter, coughing, endless complaints... The patrolmen cursed, bypassing the noise as if avoiding trouble, heading toward the distant blocks. \n\"They're gone,\" Nata lowered the curtain and announced to the sober people. \nThe workers were laying cloth strips on the ground, using charcoal sticks to write the slogans they would raise tomorrow: \"We want wages,\" \"We want rest,\" \"We want to live like human beings.\" Children huddled in the corner, dividing dry rations and small bottles of alcohol. The candlelight was dim, reflecting pairs of shining eyes. \n\"By tomorrow, will we be able to get the pay we deserve?\" an older worker asked. \n\"By tomorrow, will we be able to guarantee ten hours of rest?\" a young child asked. \n\"...Sorry, I cannot guarantee that for you,\" Nata fell silent. \n\"Our flags may fall, but every step we take forward will leave a mark on the ground.\" \nPerhaps, far away in another era, someone has already followed it until dawn.",
